; refusal-truncated-carrier: a clean three-key score. The runner packs it,
; then forms a 40-byte prefix from those exact bytes (no checked-in blob) and
; offers the prefix to PacerRt. The prefix is a decode refusal; the full
; carrier is the frame oracle.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

(track :target level
  (key :at 0b :value 0.25)
  (key :at 2b :value 0.5 :ease smoothstep)
  (key :at 4b :value 0.75 :ease in-out-cubic))
